					<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
					<string name="Name">--Read Me!--</string>
					<ProtectedString name="Source">[[
&#9;Hello lucky friends I choose to give this to
&#9;Here is how to work it:
&#9;&#9;1. For the T-shirt, you use the T-shirt&apos;s ID. Not
&#9;&#9;&#9;the texture. Change the ID using the Configuration
&#9;&#9;&#9;thingy. Just paste the ID of the T-shirt into the 
&#9;&#9;&#9;Value called, &quot;ShirtId&quot;.

&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;EXAMPLE: 50753564 would be the ID for my
&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;War of the Cliff VIP. Notice it isn&apos;t
&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;the Texture.

&#9;&#9;2. Only change things I say you can, unless your
&#9;&#9;&#9;an epic scripter. Anything you can changed has 
&#9;&#9;&#9;a &quot;--&quot; by it and a discription of what it does.

&#9;&#9;3. Please don&apos;t replublish this. I spent a long
